atible\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10 checklist completed\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling compliant with requirements\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Write one check per document pair that must agree, or delete the section when the packet holds no paired documents. GOOD: CHK-140 [P1] `plan.md` and `tasks.md` agree on the three phases. WEAK: Docs are verified. -->\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All spec documents synchronized\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation complete (if applicable)\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer documented\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n<!-- FILL: L3+ means Level 3 and above, so this section stays at Level 3. Name the real approver for each role. Delete a row when the role does not exist. Write `N/A` or delete the section when no sign-off applies. GOOD: Conductor, runs every task. Operator, merges the commit. WEAK: Signed off. -->\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Name] | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"recommend level quiet flag tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Path variables**: `S` = `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh`; `P` = `specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n## AI EXECUTION PROTOCOL\n\n### Pre-Task Checklist\nBefore starting any task, verify:\n1. [ ] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and this file were read in full\n2. [ ] The task's file is `$S`; packet docs change only when observed output contradicts them\n3. [ ] The verification command and its expected output are known before the first edit\n4. [ ] No earlier task left an uncommitted change outside the packet\n\n### Execution Rules\n\n| Rule | Requirement |\n|------|-------------|\n| TASK-SEQ | Run T001-T011 in order; T001-T002 produce the baseline that T007-T009 compare against |\n| TASK-SCOPE | Modify only `$S`; record anything else as a finding instead of editing it |\n| TASK-VERIFY | Run the task's Verify command and read its output before marking the task complete |\n| TASK-DOC | Record any deviation from this plan in `implementation-summary.md` at completion |\n\n### Status Reporting Format\n\n`[T###] [DONE | IN PROGRESS | BLOCKED] - one line naming the command and its observed result`\n\n### Blocked Task Protocol\n1. Mark the task `[B]` and state the blocking fact in one line\n2. Record the fact beside the completion criteria in this file\n3. Continue with the next unblocked task; escalate after two blocked tasks\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read `output_text()`, `show_help()` and the argument loop in `$S`. Verify: `rg -n 'Recommended Level:|--json\\|-j|show_help' \"$S\"` prints the level line, the `--json` case and the help function\n- [ ] T002 Capture the pre-change baselines under `$P/scratch/`: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural > \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` and the same invocation with `--json > \"$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt\"`. Verify: `wc -l < \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\"` prints 17 and `head -1 \"$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt\"` prints `{`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T003 Add `QUIET=false` to the globals block in `$S`, beside `JSON_OUTPUT`. Verify: `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0\n- [ ] T004 Add a `--quiet|-q` case arm to the argument loop in `$S`, setting `QUIET=true` and shifting one argument. Verify: `rg -n 'quiet' \"$S\"` prints the case arm\n- [ ] T005 Add the early quiet branch at the top of `output_text()` in `$S`: print the same `Recommended Level:` line and return before the report body. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet | wc -l` prints 1\n- [ ] T006 Document the flag in the header OPTIONS block and in `show_help()` in `$S`. Verify: `rg -n -- '--quiet' \"$S\"` prints both documentation sites\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T007 Verify the default report is unchanged. Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural)` prints nothing\n- [ ] T008 Verify JSON is unchanged with and without the flag. Verify: `diff \"$P/scratch/baseline-json.txt\" <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --json --quiet)` prints nothing\n- [ ] T009 Verify the error path: `bash \"$S\" --quiet` and `bash \"$S\" --quiet --bogus` each exit 1, write the unchanged error to stderr, and write nothing to stdout. Verify: captured stdout is empty and `$?` is 1 for both\n- [ ] T010 Verify the quiet line matches the report. Verify: `diff <(grep -m1 '^Recommended Level:' \"$P/scratch/baseline-default.txt\") <(bash \"$S\" --loc 500 --files 15 --auth --api --db --architectural --quiet)` prints nothing\n- [ ] T011 Reconcile the packet docs with the observed output; change `spec.md`, `plan.md` or this file only where the observation contradicts them\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `$P/scratch/` holds the baseline and quiet captures that T007-T010 compare against\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n## Verification Checklist\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n## Verification Protocol\n\n| Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n|----------|----------|-------------------|\n| **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n| **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n| **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n## Pre-Implementation\n\n- [ ] CHK-001 [P0] Requirements documented in spec.md\n- [ ] CHK-002 [P0] Technical approach defined in plan.md\n- [ ] CHK-003 [P1] Dependencies identified and available\n<!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n## Code Quality\n\n- [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `bash -n \"$S\"` exits 0 after every edit\n- [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No new stderr text appears in any mode\n- [ ] CHK-012 [P1] The quiet branch cannot fail independently: it prints one line and returns\n- [ ] CHK-013 [P1] The change follows the existing case-arm and global-variable patterns in `$S`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## Testing Checklist\n\n- [ ] CHK-020 [P0] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] CHK-021 [P0] A valid `--quiet` run prints exactly one line and exits 0\n- [ ] CHK-022 [P1] The mode matrix (default, `--quiet`, `--json`, `--json --quiet`) is verified\n- [ ] CHK-023 [P1] Invalid input exits 1 with unchanged stderr and empty stdout in both modes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n## Fix Completeness\n\nN/A - this packet adds a feature and closes no finding, so no finding class, producer inventory or adversarial table applies. The consumer inventory that does apply is recorded in `plan.md` under Affected Surfaces.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n## Security\n\n- [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No hardcoded secrets or credentials added\n- [ ] CHK-031 [P0] Input validation is unchanged; `--quiet` adds one boolean switch and no new input surface\n- [ ] CHK-032 [P1] Auth/authz: N/A - the script reads no identity and calls no service\n<!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n## Documentation\n\n- [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md` and this file agree on the flag name, the precedence rule and the expected output\n- [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The header comment and `show_help()` both list `--quiet`\n- [ ] CHK-042 [P2] README: N/A - the script's own help is the documented surface\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n## File Organization\n\n- [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Baseline captures live under `scratch/` only\n- [ ] CHK-051 [P1] `scratch/` holds no temporary file that verification still needs after the packet closes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## Verification Summary\n\n| Category | Total | Verified |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| P0 Items | 10 | 0/10 |\n| P1 Items | 18 | 0/18 |\n| P2 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n\n**Verification Date**: 2026-10-25\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n## L3+: Architecture Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-100 [P0] ADR-001 is followed: the quiet line renders from the same format site as the default report\n- [ ] CHK-101 [P1] ADR-002 is followed: `--json --quiet` emits the JSON document unchanged\n- [ ] CHK-102 [P1] Both ADRs carry a status and a rejected alternative with a reason\n- [ ] CHK-103 [P2] Migration path: N/A - no stored state or caller contract changes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:arch-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n## L3+: Performance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-110 [P1] The flag adds no measurable runtime (NFR-P01)\n- [ ] CHK-111 [P2] Throughput: N/A - single-shot CLI with no sustained load\n- [ ] CHK-112 [P2] Load testing: N/A - no service or shared resource\n- [ ] CHK-113 [P2] Benchmarks: not recorded; the flag adds one string comparison\n<!-- /ANCHOR:perf-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n## L3+: Deployment Readiness\n\n- [ ] CHK-120 [P0] Rollback procedure documented in `plan.md` and rerun against the three baseline comparisons\n- [ ] CHK-121 [P1] Feature flag: N/A - `--quiet` is itself the opt-in and defaults off\n- [ ] CHK-122 [P2] Monitoring: N/A - no service is deployed\n- [ ] CHK-123 [P2] Runbook: the rollback procedure in `plan.md` section 7 is the runbook\n- [ ] CHK-124 [P2] Deployment runbook review: N/A - no deploy step exists\n<!-- /ANCHOR:deploy-ready -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n## L3+: Compliance Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-130 [P1] Security review: N/A - no credential, network or data path is touched\n- [ ] CHK-131 [P1] Dependency licenses: no new dependency is added\n- [ ] CHK-132 [P2] OWASP Top 10: N/A - CLI with no web surface\n- [ ] CHK-133 [P2] Data handling: N/A - the script stores and transmits nothing\n<!-- /ANCHOR:compliance-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n## L3+: Documentation Verification\n\n- [ ] CHK-140 [P1] All packet documents agree on the flag name, precedence and one-line output\n- [ ] CHK-141 [P1] API documentation: N/A - `--help` is the CLI contract\n- [ ] CHK-142 [P2] User-facing documentation updated in the script header and help text\n- [ ] CHK-143 [P2] Knowledge transfer: the two ADRs in `plan.md` record why the branch lives in `output_text()` and why JSON wins\n<!-- /ANCHOR:docs-verify -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n## L3+: Sign-Off\n\n| Approver | Role | Status | Date |\n|----------|------|--------|------|\n| Packet operator | Technical Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n| Packet operator | Product Owner | [ ] Approved | |\n| Packet operator | QA Lead | [ ] Approved | |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:sign-off -->\n\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":86,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":82}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/217-weak-model-spec-authoring/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
